---
description: Multiplayer must keep working; server stays authoritative
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never break: room creation, room joining by code, host start, player
  nicknames, allocation sync, lock-in sync, reveal sync, disconnect handling.
  Two browsers/laptops must be able to complete a full game.
- The server (`server/src/room.ts`) is the single source of truth: it owns
  phases, timers, allocations, scores and the correct answer. Clients render
  state and send intents; they never compute outcomes locally.
- The socket contract lives in `shared/src/types.ts`
  (`ClientToServerEvents` / `ServerToClientEvents`). Any protocol change
  updates that file first and both sides together.
- Validate all client input server-side (`allocationsValid`, phase checks,
  lock checks). Exact loot splits stay private until reveal; only totals,
  lock status and confidence flags are public.
- Client effects must tolerate out-of-order/late state: cancel running
  timelines when a new question arrives, re-hydrate from
  `GameEventBridge.lastRoomState` on scene (re)start.
- After protocol or flow changes, run `node scripts/smoke-test.mjs` with the
  dev servers up to prove the two-player loop end to end.
